# UI and Visualization Guidelines

## Visualization Principles

### Core Goals

1. **Clarity** - Make thought progression easy to understand
2. **Real-time** - Update as thoughts are generated
3. **Interactive** - Allow exploration of thought trees
4. **Informative** - Show metrics and relationships

### Design Philosophy

- Minimize cognitive load
- Use familiar VS Code UI patterns
- Maintain consistency with IDE theme
- Progressive disclosure of details

## Tree View Design

### Thought Hierarchy

```
📊 Sequential Thinking Session
├── 🧠 Thought 1: Initial analysis
│   └── 📝 "Analyzing the problem..."
├── 🧠 Thought 2: Hypothesis formation
│   └── 📝 "I believe the solution is..."
├── 🔄 Thought 3: Revision of Thought 1
│   └── 📝 "Actually, reconsidering..."
└── 🌿 Branch A (from Thought 2)
    ├── 🧠 Thought 4: Alternative approach
    └── 🧠 Thought 5: Branch conclusion
```

### Icon Usage

Use VS Code codicons consistently:

- `$(lightbulb)` - Regular thought
- `$(git-branch)` - Branched thought
- `$(sync)` - Revision
- `$(check)` - Final thought (nextThoughtNeeded: false)
- `$(warning)` - Needs more thoughts
- `$(symbol-number)` - Thought number indicator

### Tree Item Properties

```typescript
class ThoughtTreeItem extends vscode.TreeItem {
  constructor(thought: Thought) {
    super(
      `Thought ${thought.thoughtNumber}: ${truncate(thought.thought)}`,
      thought.nextThoughtNeeded
        ? vscode.TreeItemCollapsibleState.Collapsed
        : vscode.TreeItemCollapsibleState.None
    );

    this.tooltip = this.createTooltip(thought);
    this.description = this.createDescription(thought);
    this.iconPath = this.selectIcon(thought);
    this.contextValue = 'thought';
  }

  private createTooltip(thought: Thought): string {
    return `Thought ${thought.thoughtNumber}/${thought.totalThoughts}\n\n${thought.thought}`;
  }

  private createDescription(thought: Thought): string {
    const tags = [];
    if (thought.isRevision) tags.push('revision');
    if (thought.branchId) tags.push(`branch:${thought.branchId}`);
    return tags.join(', ');
  }
}
```

## Webview Visualization

### Interactive Thought Graph

Display thought progression as an interactive graph:

```html
<div id="thought-graph">
  <svg width="100%" height="600">
    <!-- Nodes and edges rendered here -->
  </svg>
</div>
```

**Features:**

- Pan and zoom support
- Click nodes to view details
- Highlight revision chains
- Show branch relationships
- Display progress metrics

### Thought Detail Panel

Show detailed information for selected thought:

```html
<div class="thought-detail">
  <h3>Thought #<span id="thought-number"></span></h3>
  <div class="thought-content" id="content"></div>
  <div class="thought-metadata">
    <span class="badge">Progress: <span id="progress"></span></span>
    <span class="badge" id="status"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="thought-relations">
    <h4>Relationships</h4>
    <ul id="relations"></ul>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Styling

### Color Scheme

Respect VS Code theme variables:

```css
:root {
  --thought-primary: var(--vscode-editor-foreground);
  --thought-secondary: var(--vscode-descriptionForeground);
  --thought-accent: var(--vscode-textLink-foreground);
  --thought-warning: var(--vscode-editorWarning-foreground);
  --thought-success: var(--vscode-testing-iconPassed);
  --thought-border: var(--vscode-panel-border);
}
```

### Thought States

Visual indicators for thought states:

- **Active** - Highlighted border, primary color
- **Completed** - Checkmark, success color
- **Revision** - Orange/warning color
- **Branched** - Dotted connection line
- **Failed** - Error color, error icon

### Typography

```css
.thought-content {
  font-family: var(--vscode-editor-font-family);
  font-size: var(--vscode-editor-font-size);
  line-height: 1.6;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}

.thought-number {
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--vscode-textLink-foreground);
}
```

## Progress Indicators

### Linear Progress

Show overall thought progress:

```html
<div class="progress-bar">
  <div class="progress-fill" style="width: 60%;"></div>
  <span class="progress-text">6/10 thoughts</span>
</div>
```

### Metrics Display

```html
<div class="metrics">
  <div class="metric">
    <span class="metric-label">Total Thoughts</span>
    <span class="metric-value">10</span>
  </div>
  <div class="metric">
    <span class="metric-label">Revisions</span>
    <span class="metric-value">2</span>
  </div>
  <div class="metric">
    <span class="metric-label">Branches</span>
    <span class="metric-value">1</span>
  </div>
  <div class="metric">
    <span class="metric-label">Depth</span>
    <span class="metric-value">5</span>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Animations

Use subtle animations for updates:

```css
.thought-node {
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
}

.thought-node.new {
  animation: fadeIn 0.5s ease;
}

@keyframes fadeIn {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-10px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}
```

## Interactive Features

### Context Menus

Add context menu actions to tree items:

```typescript
// In package.json
"menus": {
  "view/item/context": [
    {
      "command": "sequential-thinking-vis.copyThought",
      "when": "view == sequentialThinkingView && viewItem == thought"
    },
    {
      "command": "sequential-thinking-vis.exportThought",
      "when": "view == sequentialThinkingView && viewItem == thought"
    }
  ]
}
```

### Hover Information

Show additional info on hover:

```typescript
provideHover(document: vscode.TextDocument, position: vscode.Position): vscode.Hover {
  return new vscode.Hover([
    `**Thought ${thought.number}**`,
    `Status: ${thought.nextThoughtNeeded ? 'In Progress' : 'Complete'}`,
    `Progress: ${thought.number}/${thought.totalThoughts}`
  ]);
}
```

## Responsive Design

Support different panel sizes:

```css
.thought-graph {
  min-width: 300px;
  max-width: 100%;
}

@media (max-width: 500px) {
  .thought-graph svg {
    height: 400px;
  }

  .metrics {
    flex-direction: column;
  }
}
```

## Accessibility

### ARIA Labels

```html
<div role="tree" aria-label="Sequential Thinking Tree">
  <div role="treeitem" aria-level="1" aria-expanded="true">Thought 1</div>
</div>
```

### Keyboard Navigation

Support keyboard controls:

- Arrow keys: Navigate tree
- Enter: Expand/collapse
- Space: Select thought
- Tab: Move between sections

### Screen Reader Support

```html
<span class="sr-only"> Thought {{number}} of {{total}}: {{content}} </span>
```

## Performance

### Virtual Scrolling

For large thought trees, implement virtual scrolling:

```typescript
class VirtualTreeProvider {
  private visibleRange = { start: 0, end: 50 };

  getChildren(element?: ThoughtNode): ThoughtNode[] {
    if (!element) {
      // Return only visible root nodes
      return this.rootNodes.slice(this.visibleRange.start, this.visibleRange.end);
    }
    return element.children;
  }
}
```

### Debounced Updates

Prevent excessive re-renders:

```typescript
private updateDebounced = debounce(() => {
  this._onDidChangeTreeData.fire(undefined);
}, 100);
```

## Export Formats

Support exporting visualizations:

- **Markdown** - Formatted thought tree
- **JSON** - Raw thought data
- **SVG** - Thought graph image
- **HTML** - Interactive visualization

## Best Practices

1. **Theme compatibility** - Always use VS Code CSS variables
2. **Efficient rendering** - Update only changed nodes
3. **Clear hierarchy** - Use indentation and icons
4. **Meaningful labels** - Descriptive node text
5. **Responsive feedback** - Immediate UI updates
6. **Graceful degradation** - Handle missing data
7. **Consistent spacing** - Follow VS Code spacing conventions
8. **Loading states** - Show spinners for async operations
